
Chili "cake" was something I came up with one time, over 20 years ago. My son, now in his 30s, has been asking for me to make it again ever since.

I finally made it again this evening. The feedback I got was all along the lines of "Oh my lord! This is so good!" 

Here's what I did.

First make up a batch of elk chili. I came up with the elk chili recipe on this list, just for this "cake".

On a large, kinda' oven-save, dinner plate. 

Stack up like lasagna.
 
Flour tortilla.
Spread chili across the top.
Spread shredded cheese over this.

Next flour tortilla.
Spread chili across the top.
Spread shredded cheese over this.

Keep layering 'till you run out of chili.

Put shredded cheese over the top of the last tortilla.

Pop it in the oven 350 for about 4..6 minutes.

Pull it out and when it cools sprinkles some chopped green onions over the top.

Enjoy!